        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq2Ik7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArBcQAKWKvuW0OEpNJrsRuNk0t5lv\nQ8eUAYdPDp0kgD3IuYWNL3Vstr3SOpbYMeVDWP9gHRw9tOffThmu1Mi9uCARM+YL\nB8E5YlQNi4BpoVLAehi1r+Al0fAd/ODgY558yAG3JvagFqhjRVknv3DH3BUXLIFe\nAnkGzQacpU0/09+MXYrDGvf7fnll9j9EwugPT6FcJtaowv0WJ7JvcRFyiMgzTPDl\nxWqGHeMSpmyYbfrRZp0/ZOsaIp4XywvlIERqgP6blaW5tN/so+dTP67+nwspeZxg\nDoSoPqVmkAt22ASW5n/inryNXTk//CAPbfgQskPjeTM+PHoTJLVBRXAUywz7H4S3\nbwFKTBhLvtPqOfKlfHlIdm26iovDCkg6me7Kym6DFY1/OPc14HMLvhYXp0h2Cwf9\nX5ltnDOQ9dwW010m7nTFcpcqmfnCMruABQ12oDh6nMtOkwryYnzzLPSh/hE0Rug4\ndduNz4F5Ifwj8nOqNxNKmv3uMJNfkXVOd2VxHJ9B93McI1nHdun+l5Qap3G6n/pP\n0Ul1y30i2Q1KGeC/AeIom9UofexJQvNzFVV90zYK/RMVrcl7ipN4ba3WM7mJd/qg\nMZhaJC9jTwxFiP6y7VANiohibuxRjLM/GYeyq3SBFPqWKf/1MZJhJURJQFApkF0d\nFlgEDR0+4VpgMxHrtczH\n=j3kP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 29492ca1d2a89ef3b9e6fefaf2a8ee826f2170be\nparent c2f6e683d3bd27017686a924e989f61aa77c1656\nauthor July-X <over618@163.com> 1792575803 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792575803 +0800\n\nfix(minimax-bot): sort the job rows before the fold takes them, clarify the README (#52)\n\n* fix(minimax-bot): order the job rows by how far along they are\n\nThe fold of the job queue kept the rows in the order the jobs arrived\nin, and only used the status to decide which three rows stay in the\nopen. A queued job could therefore sit above a job that was already\nworking, and the strip read as if the queue had not started.\n\nThe rows are sorted before the fold takes the first three now: the jobs\nthat are already working come first, the ones waiting for another job\nnext, the queued ones last. The sort is stable, so jobs of the same\nkind keep the order they arrived in.\n\nA strip that fits in the open rows has nothing to fold and keeps the\norder the official build draws, so the rows of a quiet chat are the\nofficial ones.\n\n* docs(minimax-bot): say what the fold of the job queue actually does\n\nThe Background work paragraph said the strip folds \"when more than three\nare queued\". The fold counts every job the strip lists, the ones that\nare already working included, and it keeps the first three of them in\nthe open. The sentence now says that.\n\n* chore(minimax-bot): bump the version to 0.7.7\n\n* fix(minimax-bot): sort the job rows by status and by arrival\n\nThe rows of the strip were sorted only while the fold was in play, so a\nqueued job could sit above a job that was already working when three\njobs or fewer were listed, and the rows swapped places when the fourth\none arrived. The strip sorts them now, always.\n\nThe status comes first: the jobs already working, then the ones waiting\nfor another job, then the queued ones. Jobs of the same kind are\nordered by the time they arrived, which is the moment they started or\nthe moment they were queued. A status the strip does not know yet comes\nlast, so a new one cannot scramble the order.\n\n* docs(minimax-bot): say how the strip orders the jobs it lists\n\nThe Background work paragraph described the fold but not the order the\nrows are in. It now says that the strip orders the jobs by how far\nalong they are and keeps the first three in the open.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: 4Dim <m4java@163.com>",
